<title>JAPAN: Japan August aluminium imports up 3.5 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan August aluminium imports up 3.5 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's refined aluminium imports in August were 237,155 tonnes, up 3.5 percent from 229,103 tonnes in the same month a year earlier, Finance Ministry statistics released on Monday showed.</p>
<p>The breakdown was as follows (on a customs-cleared basis, in tonnes):</p>
<p>		 August 96	  July 96    August 95</p>
<p> Total	  237,155	   252,259     229,103</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Brazil	  50,566	    18,060	40,788</p>
<p> Russia	  38,475	    46,000	24,306</p>
<p> Australia     34,589	    30,510	29,804</p>
<p> U.S.	    21,550	    41,453	19,452</p>
<p>Refined aluminium imports in the first eight months of 1996 were 1,812,974 tonnes, off 7.5 percent from 1,959,247 tonnes in the same period last year. -- Tokyo Commodities Desk (81-3 3432 6179)</p>
</text>
